                "senderName": "NWS Sacramento CA",
                "headline": "Heat Advisory issued October 3 at 2:14PM PDT until October 7 at 10:00PM PDT by NWS Sacramento CA",
                "description": "* WHAT...High temperatures of 94 to 102 degrees expected and low\ntemperatures in the mid 60s to low 70s, with widespread Moderate\nHeatRisk and areas of Major HeatRisk.\n\n* WHERE...Sacramento and northern San Joaquin valleys, Delta and\nCarquinez Strait, and foothills.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM PDT Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Hot temperatures may cause heat illnesses, especially to\nanyone without effective cooling and/or adequate hydration.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Hottest days expected Monday through\nWednesday.",
                "instruction": "Drink plenty of fluids, stay in an air-conditioned room, stay out of\nthe sun, and check up on relatives and neighbors.\n\nTake extra precautions when outside. Wear lightweight and loose\nfitting clothing. Try to limit strenuous activities to early morning\nor evening. Take action when you see symptoms of heat exhaustion and\nheat stroke.",
                "response": "Execute",
